; A fairground of moving footing (issue #54, #52's RotatingPlatform, both
; modes). Everything between the two edges tips or turns; only the shoulders
; the players start on and a small hub in the middle hold still.
;
; **Shoulders.** x=+-590..+-790, top y=300: the only fixed ground at the
; edges, and where all four spawns sit, so the round opens on still footing
; and nobody's first second is a slide.
;
; **See-saws.** Centred x=+-380 on y=300, 300 px long (x=+-230..+-530), tilt
; capped at 20 degrees so a lone player tips one without being poured off
; it. They are the dependable route: 60 px from a shoulder's lip, 140 px
; from the hub's, both inside every weapon's hook-and-fling. Standing on the
; far end of one lifts the other end -- a fight on a see-saw is also a fight
; over which way it leans.
;
; **Hub and spinner.** The hub (x=-90..90, top y=300) is fixed ground, but a
; 260 px bar spins over it at 25 deg/s about (0,140). Its tips sweep down to
; y=270, so about every 7 s the bar comes round vertical and swats anyone
; standing on the hub; in between it passes flat, and for a moment it is
; the stage's high ground. It is a timed hazard first and footing second,
; which is the only way a spinner reads fairly.
;
; Rising floor (ADR-0012) climbs to the spawns' height and takes the
; see-saws, hub and shoulders together.

